## Rust standard library runtime attribution

The distributed executable includes the Rust standard library. Its upstream
library copyright/license document is reproduced verbatim from the digest-pinned
Rust1.99.1 release compiler as `install/RUST-STDLIB-NOTICES.html` in project source
and `RUST-STDLIB-NOTICES.html` alongside this NOTICE in installed documentation.
It includes the upstream library component graph, including platform-specific
components; it is not an assertion that all of those components are linked.

Release metadata generation checks the document against the actual compiler's
`share/doc/rust/COPYRIGHT-library.html`; the build manifest records its checksum.
When changing the pinned release compiler, update this document verbatim from
that compiler before building. The SPDX asset intentionally inventories the
complete Cargo.lock registry graph, not compiler/standard-library or OS packages.

The package's standard `copyright` file also contains the complete project and
locked-crate license texts plus a plain-text rendering of all upstream Rust
library notice text. This preserves licensing when an administrator's dpkg policy
filters other documentation; the original HTML remains verbatim in the package,
source and tar archives. Package scripts do not override that system policy.
